    "reason": "evidence sufficient (proxy gate verdict; the open aspects need proposals): [ev-ebdf9bd62d77] says Kyverno Service API calls now support custom HTTP request headers, for example an Authorization token. The rendered CRD diffs [ev-99b53074f2f0] [ev-4223a9a83b9a] [ev-ca8925aad7a2] [ev-60b490ef3d10] [ev-9636947e7fb1] show what was added: a new optional field, apiCall.service.headers, which is a list of key/value pairs. It appears in the context entries of ClusterPolicy, Policy, the cleanup policies and GlobalContextEntry, and is absent before 1.13.0. Because the field is new and opt-in, and the evidence states nothing that breaks for existing setups, the open applicability aspect can be written: no existing environment is exposed (only policies that choose to use apiCall.service could adopt it), and the consequence is none/informational.",
